Notes

1 Central vision refers to vision in the straight-ahead direction, in centre of the field of vision, where the colours and details are the clearest.

2 Vection refers to the perception of self-motion in the absence of physical movement.

3 In this paper, augmented reality displays are referred as optical see-through displays such as Head-Up Displays (HUDs) or Head Mounted Displays (HMDs), where the information is projected through a transparent surface (e.g. prism, window, windscreen).

4 Inattentional blindness can be described as the fact of becoming unaware of visual changes in the field of vision, especially when being focused on a visually demanding task.
